// The contract of ode_left_last (doubling.ode). `left_chunks` is ../../../kcheck/blake3.spec's own definition:
// `the greatest power of two k with 1024 * k < len(bytes)`. The contract says where the block lies by that
// definition, for a message of any length from 1025 bytes on. The loop has no invariant: the verifier
// walks it, one path for each count the left part can have, and on each path the proof answers which
// powers of two are too great for the message. `trace depends on len`: how often the loop is gone round
// and where the block is read depend on the length, and on no byte of the message.
contract ode_left_last(h: cv, input: len bytes, len: number) {
    requires disjoint(h, input, 1)
    requires len >= 1025
    ensures h = compress(h, words(input[1024 * left_chunks(input) - 64 .. 1024 * left_chunks(input)]), counter(0), 64, 0)
    trace depends on len
    stack 64
    needs sse41
}
